# Full-Stack Kubernetes Project on AWS

## Overview

This project demonstrates a production-style, three-tier application deployment on Kubernetes using AWS. The architecture includes a simple frontend served by NGINX, a Node.js backend API, and a MySQL database managed as a StatefulSet with persistent storage.

The solution is designed to showcase modern Kubernetes deployment patterns such as:

- Containerized microservice deployment
- Service-based internal networking
- External access through NGINX Ingress
- Secret and ConfigMap-based configuration management
- Stateful database persistence with PVC-backed storage
- Docker image build and push workflow

## Architecture

The application follows a standard three-tier pattern:

User Browser
  ↓
Ingress Controller
  ↓
Frontend Service
  ↓
NGINX Frontend Pod
  ↓
Backend Service
  ↓
Node.js Backend Pod
  ↓
MySQL StatefulSet
  ↓
PVC → PV

## Technology Stack

- Frontend: NGINX serving static HTML
- Backend: Node.js + Express
- Database: MySQL 8.0
- Orchestration: Kubernetes
- External routing: NGINX Ingress Controller
- Cloud platform: AWS
- Containerization: Docker

